To incorporate the NOOP and DELE commands into the sequence of client requests, we can place the NOOP command after the LIST command and the DELE command after the MKD command. Here’s the modified sequence:

```
USER ubuntu
PASS ubuntu
SYST
PWD
PORT 127,0,0,1,132,209
LIST
NOOP
MKD test
DELE test_file.txt  ; (Assuming you want to delete a file named 'test_file.txt')
QUIT
```

This sequence maintains the logical flow of operations, where NOOP can be used as a keep-alive command after listing files, and DELE can be used after creating a directory or before quitting, depending on your needs

